codex
The publication generator crashes on an existing episode with narration in block 0, and the preview command ignores its square-rendering flag. Both issues should be corrected before considering the patch correct.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Account for voiced block 0 when mapping publication segments — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\scripts\pub.py:132-137
  When the source episode has narration on block 0, `voix.textes(ep)` keeps that block, but this mapping unconditionally subtracts one from selected indexes. For example, `episodes/2026-09-21-franchises-medicales` maps blocks 8 and 9 to the voices of blocks 7 and 8, then fails the alignment assertion. Use the same block-0 offset as `voix.textes` or reject this input explicitly.

- [P2] Keep the preview flag separate from the path variable — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\scripts\apercu.py:35-41
  In the normal documented invocation without `--carre`, the loop reassigns the boolean `carre` flag to a `Path` at line 35; paths are truthy, so line 41 always runs `render_carre.py`. This makes every preview render the square version unnecessarily and can cause a preview to fail on square-only layout issues.
The publication generator crashes on an existing episode with narration in block 0, and the preview command ignores its square-rendering flag. Both issues should be corrected before considering the patch correct.

